window.SEARCH_INDEX=[{"url": ".", "title": "Starwell Holdings", "text": "Dream with Starwell. A private holding company. We acquire and operate IT services companies in Israel, invest in real estate, and hold positions in public and private markets. ↓ What We Do Starwell IT Services Acquiring and operating IT Services businesses. Learn More → Starwell Real Estate Development and GP investments in Israel, select co-investments. Learn More → Starwell Capital Long-term investment portfolio across public markets and direct private positions. Learn More → About Starwell Learn more about Starwell About Us →"}, {"url": "our-story", "title": "About Us", "text": "About Us Starwell Holdings Starwell Holdings is a private holding company. We build and acquire operating businesses in IT services, invest in and develop real estate, and allocate capital to public markets and alternative investments. Beyond capital allocation, Starwell acts as a long-term owner and active partner - acquiring companies, scaling platforms, and working alongside management teams to develop durable businesses and real assets. Our approach combines entrepreneurial execution with disciplined investment principles. We focus on opportunities where long-term ownership, operational involvement, and alignment with partners can create enduring value across cycles and generations. Starwell Holdings was founded by Amit Kochavi, who serves as Chairman and CEO. Meet the team → Business Focus Our activities span three core areas: IT Services We build platforms in IT services - acquiring controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable companies and rolling them up into a larger group. We partner with owners and operators to preserve what works while adding the infrastructure and discipline of a platform built to last. Real Estate We work in real estate in three ways: advisory mandates, participation in development projects alongside the developers running them, and limited partner investments in funds and assets. Capital We allocate capital across public equities, hedge funds, and alternative investments with a long-term mindset, complementing our operating activities. Strategy Our model is simple: operate where we have an edge, allocate where we don’t. Acquire and compound We prefer buying established, profitable businesses over starting from scratch - then compounding them, through operational improvement and further acquisitions. Proven cash flows, existing customer relationships, and experienced teams are the foundation; our job is to strengthen them, not replace them. Decentralized operations, centralized capital Portfolio companies run independently under their own management. What’s centralized is capital allocation: cash generated across the group is redeployed to its highest and best use, wherever that may be. Permanent ownership We have no fund cycles, no exit deadlines, and no pressure to sell. This lets us make decisions on a horizon measured in decades, hold through cycles, and be the buyer of choice for owners who care what happen"}, {"url": "our-history", "title": "Our History", "text": "Our History Legacy Starwell builds on four generations of entrepreneurship, capital stewardship, and civic leadership - across Los Angeles, New York, and Tel Aviv. Max Factor The entrepreneurial root of the family traces to Max Factor , who built one of the defining consumer brands of the 20th century. From a single Los Angeles shop, he transformed the global cosmetics industry through invention, craftsmanship, and an uncompromising standard of quality - proof that enduring businesses are built product by product, customer by customer. Max Factor Max Factor David M. Heyman David M. Heyman David M. Heyman The tradition of disciplined capital stewardship runs through David M. Heyman , a New York financier and philanthropist who led the New York Foundation for decades. He treated capital as an instrument of long-term responsibility - to institutions, to communities, and to the generations that follow. Real assets, two cities The family’s real estate roots run in parallel on both sides of the ocean. In Los Angeles, Herb Glaser - attorney turned developer - built Glaser Development Company into a commercial real estate developer across Southern California and the Western United States, spanning logistics centers, warehouses, and multifamily properties, alongside decades of leadership in the city’s civic and Jewish institutions. In Tel Aviv, the Buchman family built a textile enterprise and converted it into real estate holdings that grew with the city itself. That tradition continues today through Doron Kochavi , attorney and real estate developer. Doron Kochavi Starwell Starwell is the modern expression of these roots: a private holding company that acquires and builds operating businesses, develops real assets, and allocates capital for the long term. The underlying values are inherited, not invented - integrity, patient ownership, and the responsibility to build things that endure."}, {"url": "our-team", "title": "Our Team", "text": "Our Team Leadership Amit Kochavi Chairman, CEO & Founder Amit founded Starwell Holdings to build a private investment and operating company that combines long-term capital with operational execution. He served in the Israeli Air Force’s Ofek technology unit. In 2019 he founded Circles I.T. Innovation Ltd., which merged its operations with Doss in 2025. He was named to Forbes Israel 30 Under 30 in 2017 and to TheMarker 40 Under 40 in 2025. He is Senior Advisor to the Mayor of Sderot, a member of the President of Israel’s Kol HaAm Council, and a member of the Board of Governors of Sapir Academic College. Amit continues to grow Starwell’s portfolio of platforms and partnerships, focused on building enduring value across cycles and geographies. LinkedIn X Shirly Gur Arie Executive Assistant Shirly supports Starwell’s leadership and day-to-day operations, coordinating across the firm’s platforms and partners to keep the organization running smoothly. LinkedIn"}, {"url": "technology", "title": "Starwell IT Services", "text": "Starwell IT Services Acquiring controlling or significant stakes in IT services companies, in Israel and beyond. The Thesis The IT services market is large, growing, and highly fragmented. Most of it consists of independent companies built on expertise and long-standing client relationships, without the backing of a larger group. In a technology landscape that never stops changing - cloud migration, artificial intelligence, and successive waves of transformation - businesses need a trusted external technology partner more than ever. Starwell IT Services acquires controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable IT services companies. We partner with owners and operators to preserve what works, while building around them the infrastructure and discipline of a platform built to last. 01 Acquire Controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable IT services companies. 02 Integrate Central systems, shared infrastructure, and a consistent standard of service across the portfolio. 03 Grow Operational improvement, talent development, and expanded service capabilities, driving long-term value creation. Acquisition criteria Established and profitable Israeli IT services companies with a history of profitable operation. Scale Annual revenue in the tens of millions of shekels, with teams of dozens of employees. Stake Controlling or significant stakes. Continuity We keep management, employees, and client relationships in place. Owners considering a sale are welcome to contact us in full confidence. Contact us → What owners can expect Permanent ownership We buy to hold. The companies we acquire are not packaged for resale. No fund clock We have no fund cycles and no exit deadlines, so there is no pressure to sell. A fast and discreet process A small team, direct conversations, and confidentiality at every stage. Team Tal Raif Investor and Board Member [TBD: bio, from Tal’s LinkedIn] LinkedIn"}, {"url": "real-estate", "title": "Starwell Real Estate", "text": "Starwell Real Estate Development and strategic real estate investment across Israel and the United States. Markets Israel Development & Advisory Residential and mixed-use development in Tel Aviv and central Israel, alongside institutional developers and public-sector partners. Focus on urban renewal and projects with structural demand tailwinds. United States Capital Allocation Limited partner investments in value-add multifamily and industrial logistics strategies, alongside institutional operators with demonstrated track records. Starwell Positions held by Starwell: advisory mandates, participation in development, and limited partner investments. Urban Renewal Rova 7 - Mevoot Yafo ● Tel Aviv, Israel ■ Strategic Advisory - municipality relations, commercial concept, and marketing strategy △ Keren Reality, Kardan Real Estate (50/50 JV) 55-dunam urban renewal project encompassing approximately 890 residential units, 5,000 sqm of commercial space, 20,000 sqm of office space, and 12 dunams of public area. Approved master plan (May 2023). Multifamily The Dawson ● Cartersville, Georgia, US ■ Limited Partner △ Wilpon & Co. 192-unit multifamily value-add acquisition. Industrial Logistics Terminal Logistics Fund II ● US Logistics Markets ■ Limited Partner △ Center Capital Partners Private real estate fund focused on industrial logistics assets across US markets. Website → Family track record Projects developed by Doron Kochavi. These are not Starwell holdings; they are included as background to the family’s work in real estate. Tel Aviv Beyond Towers ● Tel Aviv, Israel ■ Advisory & Owner Representative (Doron Kochavi) △ Tidhar Group, Union Group, Himnuta–KKL Large-scale mixed-use development comprising office, residential, and commercial space. Total project value estimated at NIS 4–4.5 billion. Portfolio Kochavi Real Estate Portfolio ● Tel Aviv, Israel ■ Portfolio-level management, advisory, and future development planning △ Developer: Doron Kochavi Multi-decade development and investment portfolio built by Doron Kochavi, encompassing over 750 units across more than 20 buildings in Tel Aviv."}, {"url": "capital", "title": "Starwell Capital", "text": "Starwell Capital Long-term investment portfolio across public markets and direct private positions. Approach Patient, conviction-driven capital allocation across public markets and direct private positions. Starwell Capital holds the group’s investment portfolio outside the operating companies. The mandate spans long-term public market holdings and direct private positions, including private equity, selective hedge fund allocations, and real estate. We invest with a long time horizon and concentrate where we have genuine conviction. Starwell invests only its own capital and does not manage third-party funds or solicit investments. 01 Private Equity Private equity investments in buy-out and roll-up strategies, acquiring and improving traditional businesses through operational, financial, and technological efficiency. 02 Public Markets Long-term concentrated holdings in public companies where the firm has deep conviction in the business and management team. 03 Hedge Funds Selective allocations to long-strategy hedge funds with differentiated process and consistent risk-adjusted performance. 04 Real Estate Capital allocations to real estate funds and structures as part of a diversified long-term portfolio. Portfolio Pioneers - Healthcare Staffing AI Roll-Up Role: Investor AI-native roll-up of healthcare staffing agencies, modernizing legacy operators with proprietary AI to automate workflows and dramatically improve recruiter output. Website → Kodiak Holdings Role: Investor A long-term partner for aspiring small business owners, backing the next generation of American owner-operators with equity financing and support across due diligence, transaction structuring, capital raising, and ongoing operations. Website → Legion Holdings Role: Investor AI-native growth buyout firm investing in business services companies, modernizing their operations with AI, and compounding value through disciplined M&A. Website →"}, {"url": "news", "title": "News", "text": "News News & Insights Company news, market commentary, and updates on our investments. Latest All Company News Real Estate Company News Jun 3, 2025 Circles Merges Operations with U.S.-Based Doss Circles is merging its operations with U.S.-based Doss and will become the Israeli sales and marketing center for the company. Read More → Real Estate May 6, 2025 Lee & Associates Atlanta Facilitates Sale of 28-Acre Industrial Site to Terminal Logistics Center Capital's IOS platform, Terminal Logistics, has acquired a 28-acre site in Gainesville, GA. Read More →"}, {"url": "contact", "title": "Contact", "text": "Contact Get in Touch For inquiries about investment opportunities, partnerships, or potential transactions, please complete the form below. A member of our team will respond promptly. Leave empty: First Name * Last Name * Organization Email * Subject Message Submit Offices Givatayim Beyond Towers Ariel Sharon Street 1 Givatayim, Israel Los Angeles 11601 Wilshire Blvd #2080 Los Angeles, CA 90025 USA"}, {"url": "careers", "title": "Careers", "text": "Join Us Careers at Starwell We’re a small, high-conviction team building platforms across IT Services and Real Estate, with passive capital allocation to public markets and alternative assets. We look for people who think long-term and operate with precision. How We Work Long-Term Thinking We build for decades, not quarters. Every decision is made with durability and permanence in mind. Operational Excellence We get into the details. Great outcomes come from rigorous execution and deep domain knowledge. Integrity We say what we mean and do what we say - with partners, portfolio companies, and each other. Entrepreneurial Spirit We are builders. We back people who create things that didn’t exist before. Working with us We do not run a standing job board. We hire when we meet the right person, so we read everything that reaches us. Send a CV and a short note about the work you want to do to shirly@starwellholdings.com . Get in Touch"}, {"url": "privacy", "title": "Privacy Policy", "text": "Legal Privacy Policy Draft. This policy is pending legal review and is not yet in force. Who we are Starwell Holdings Ltd., Company No. 517166237. Registered address: [TBD]. What we collect If you write to us through the contact form we receive the first and last name, organization, email address, subject and message you enter. We do not ask for any other personal detail, and the site does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Why we hold it To read your message and reply to it. Legal basis: [TBD]. Who processes it Form submissions are handled by our hosting provider’s form service and reach us by email. Further processors, and any transfer of data outside Israel: [TBD]. How long we keep it [TBD] Your rights Rights of access, correction and deletion, and the procedure for exercising them: [TBD]. Contact Questions about this policy: amit@starwellholdings.com . Last updated: [TBD]."}, {"url": "accessibility", "title": "Accessibility Statement", "text": "Legal Accessibility Statement Draft. This statement is pending legal review and is not yet in force. Our commitment Starwell Holdings Ltd. works to keep this website usable by as many people as possible, including people using assistive technology. Standard Standard applied and level of conformance: [TBD]. What has been done The site is built with semantic HTML and landmark regions, can be operated by keyboard, keeps text and background contrast high in both the light and dark colour schemes, labels every image and form field, respects the operating system’s reduced-motion setting, and reflows to a single column on small screens without horizontal scrolling. Known limitations [TBD] Accessibility coordinator Name, telephone and email: [TBD]. Reporting a problem If you run into an accessibility problem on this site, please write to amit@starwellholdings.com and tell us the page and what happened. Date of this statement: [TBD]."}, {"url": "sitemap", "title": "Sitemap", "text": "Sitemap Sitemap Every page on the Starwell Holdings website, organized in one place. Company Home About Us Our Team Our History News Careers What We Do IT Services Real Estate Capital Resources Contact Search Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Sitemap עברית"}];
